gantt
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: the other diagrams show the order of steps. How long does each step take for one contract, and in which fiscal year does each step occur?
  %% IDEA: one contract extends over three calendar years. Its budget is prepared in the year before, the work is done in the budget year, and the last payment and the audit occur in the year after. The four sections are the four lines of steps of diagram 00d: authority, the thing bought, cash, records.
  %% THE EXAMPLE IS INVENTED. The agency, the amounts and the dates of the single steps are not real. The rules that fix the earliest and latest dates are real, and they are listed here with their sources.
  %% THE EXAMPLE: an agency builds a school building for PHP 48 million. The amount is a capital outlay in the FY 2026 budget law, without a pre-condition for release. The work takes nine months and is billed in three parts.
  %% RULES USED, WITH SOURCES: the agency may hold the bidding before the budget law exists, once the President's budget is submitted, but it may not award before the funding is in effect and the head of the agency has approved the final procurement plan [IRR12009 s.12][RA12009 s.12]. The FY 2026 budget law took effect on 5 January 2026, and the law itself is the allotment for items without pre-conditions [NBC599]. Award within 60 days from the opening of bids, contract within 10 days after the award, notice to proceed within 3 days [RA12009]. A regular NCA lapses at the end of its quarter, and the regular NCA of a later period also covers payables of earlier years [NBC599 s.4.2]. The bank credits the payee within two banking days after it receives the payment order [CL2018-14]. Quarterly reports within 30 days after each quarter, and the report on unpaid obligations within 30 days after the year [JC2019-1]. Year-end statements to COA by 14 February, annual report of COA by 30 September [PD1445 s.41]. Capital outlays of FY 2026 may be obligated until 31 December 2027 (the table in my copy was partly unreadable) [NBC599 s.3.3].
  %% WHERE THE EXAMPLE FAILS ON PURPOSE: the third bill is accepted on 20 November 2026, but the cash authority of the fourth quarter is fully used. The supplier is paid on 15 February 2027. During these weeks the amount is an expense and a payable in the books, an obligation in the registry, and no disbursement. Diagram 08c explains these three measures.
  %% GENERAL KNOWLEDGE, NOT OPENED IN A SOURCE HERE: the dates of the budget preparation in 2025 (the pattern of 2026 is used), the recording of the building as an asset at final acceptance, and the month in which the audit report of the agency is issued.
